Libraries and tools used by the engine include Haxe, Neko, hxcpp, Lime,
OpenFL, HaxeFlixel and its addons, flixel-animate, funkin-modchart, HScript,
hscript-ex, HScript Iris, TJSON, Away3D, hxvlc/libVLC, discord-rpc, and astcenc.
Their distributions retain their own licences. The portable ASTC decoder's
Apache 2.0 licence accompanies the decoder in tools/astcenc-LICENSE.txt.

The Flx3D compatibility code is derived from Codename Engine-Dev and retains
its source attribution. Its Apache 2.0 licence is at
 tools/licenses/CodenameEngine-Dev-LICENSE.txt in the source checkout, or
 licenses/CodenameEngine-Dev-LICENSE.txt in the Windows release.

Compatibility work uses Codename Engine, Psych Engine, Nightmare Vision,
Modding Plus/Poop and FNF V-Slice behavior as references. Those projects and
all mod authors retain credit for their original code and content.

